custom assertions) - Cost: essentially free (<1ms) - Must pass before ANY LLM-based verification #### L3: Single-Agent Self-Verification - Chain-of-Verification: plan→draft→verify→refine - Self-consistency: sample multiple times, check agreement - Step-by-step verification for reasoning chains - +28% FACTSCORE, +23% F1 on QA tasks - Cost: 2x tokens (generation + verification) - When to use: reasoning-heavy tasks, open-ended generation #### L4: Multi-Agent Cross-Verification - LLM-as-Judge: separate model scores output quality - Reflexion: agent reflects on own output, identifies issues - Adversarial Debate (DebateCV): multiple agents argue, consensus wins - 2.6-5.8% accuracy improvement - Corrects misinterpretation, overlooked evidence, speculation - Process Verification: verify each step, not just final output - Cost: 3-5x tokens (multiple agents) - When to use: critical decisions, high-stakes outputs #### L5: Source Grounding & Rollback - Citation verification: every claim must cite source - Git-like checkpointing: save state at each verification gate - Rollback procedures: revert to last verified state - Immutable audit trail: every decision logged with hash chain - External fact-checking integration (where available) - When to use: compliance-required tasks, factual claims ### 3. The 5-3-1 Governance Stack #### 3.1 Five Hardening Patterns 1. **Bounded Loops**: max_iterations, max_tokens, max_time per task 2. **Circuit Breakers**: detect failure patterns, open circuit, fallback 3. **Idempotent Tools**: safe retries, no double side effects 4. **Human-in-the-Loop Gates**: approval for high-risk actions 5. **Immutable Audit Logs**: complete chain of causality #### 3.2 Three Governance Tiers - **Tier 1 — Sandbox**: Process/container isolation, file system restrictions, network policies - **Tier 2 — Pipeline**: AutoHarness 6-step (Parse→Risk→Permission→Execute→Sanitize→Audit) - **Tier 3 — Access Control**: RBAC + ABAC + ReBAC, Cedar/SpiceDB integration #### 3.3 One Immutable Audit Trail - Hash-chained logging (SHA-256) - Identity-bound: every action attributed to agent + human approver - Digital signatures for critical operations - EU AI Act Art. 12 compliance (6-month retention) - Tamper-evident: any modification breaks hash chain ### 4. Cost-Optimized Verification - Model cascading for verification: Haiku (L1-L2) → Sonnet (L3-L4) → Opus (L5) - Batch verification questions for parallel execution - Hard max_retries=3 with human escalation - Skip unnecessary layers based on task risk profile - Expected cost: 1.5-3x base generation cost (not 5-15x with naive approach) ### 5. Failure Mode Taxonomy & Response Matrix | Failure | Detection | Response | Layer | |---------|-----------|----------|-------| | Schema violation | L2 validation | Auto-retry with corrected format | L2 | | Hallucinated tool | L1 structured output | Reject + tool RAG reselection | L1+L2 | | Wrong reasoning | L3 self-verify | Re-generate with corrected chain | L3 | | Factual error | L4 debate + L5 grounding | Ground in sources + re-verify | L4+L5 | | Context drift | Memory gate check | Reload from folder memory | Memory | | Tool misuse | L2 permission check | Escalate to human | L2+Tier3 | | Infinite loop | Bounded loop counter | Circuit breaker + fallback | Pattern1 | | Cascading failure | Cross-agent monitoring | Kill switch + ring isolation | Pattern2 | ### 6. OWASP Agentic AI 15 Threat Coverage Map Map each of the 15 threats to Adaptoid countermeasures: T1 Memory Poisoning → L5 source grounding + audit trail T2 Tool Misuse → L2 permission checks + Tool RAG T3... (cover all 15) ### 7. Production Incident Prevention - Amazon Kiro analysis: permission escalation + no HITL gate - PocketOS analysis: credential exposure + no sandbox - Common patterns: 24-point prevention checklist ### 8. Verification Gate Templates Provide 3 reusable templates: - Template A: Lightweight (L1+L2 only) — for prototyping - Template B: Standard (L1+L2+L3) — for most production tasks - T