After setup, the agent reads the folder’s key files (see Folder Structure below) and is ready to ingest a PROJECT-INTENT.md. In seconds it will generate a tailored execution plan and begin work within the hardened Adaptoid environment.

Folder-Based Persistent OS Architecture
The Adaptoid workspace uses a folder-based context architecture to enforce persistent memory and context loading on every session. This is akin to the Claude Folder Structure pioneered in 2026: instead of ephemeral prompts, all critical knowledge and rules live in well-defined files that the agent “reads before it writes.” The recommended layout under the top-level directory (Adaptoid-OS/) is:

